.TH SKOGAI-MODULE-BUILD 1  "skogai-module-build 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai\-module\-build \- build `skogai` for a shell: one argc file with every module, man pages, completions
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai module build\fR [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.br
build `skogai` for a shell: one argc file with every module, man pages, completions
.br

.br
writes into <local|global dir>/tmp/skogai/, throwaway and rebuilt at will:
.br
bin/skogai (help and completion for core and every module found from here;
.br
everything runs through the bin/skogai that built it), completions/skogai.sh
.br
for ARGC_COMPLETIONS_PATH, completions/skogai.{bash,zsh,fish}, man/man1.
.br
prints the env lines that put it on PATH, MANPATH and ARGC_COMPLETIONS_PATH.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR=\fITO\fR
.br
where to build, default core.module.install
.br

.br
[\fIpossible values: \fRlocal, global]
.TP
\fB\-\-shell\fR=\fISHELL\fR
.br
env lines for this shell, default from $SHELL
.br

.br
[\fIpossible values: \fRbash, zsh, fish]
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
Print help
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES:"
.TP
\fISKOGAI_SYSTEM_DIR\fR [default: /etc/skogai]
.br
dir of the system layer config
.TP
\fISKOGAI_CONFIG_DIR\fR
.br
dir of the global layer, default ~/.config/skogai
.TP
\fISKOGAI_LOCAL_DIR\fR [default: .skogai]
.br
dir of the local layer; relative is from the git root, or pwd
.TP
\fISKOGAI_MODULE_PATH\fR
.br
colon\-separated dirs of module sources, default the one this module sits in
